{"title":"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> matrix whose entries come from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e8486f10ccfc6d9b79d811cf46cc27c8abc9094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S={1,2,...,2n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> is called a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7baf291918cbe45c396bc3a7145870db3b39c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{silver}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> matrix if, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00340aba36745c22e8873fefef2b76a9f89b8aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,2,...,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th row and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th column together contain all elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.  Show that\n</p><p>(a) there is no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7baf291918cbe45c396bc3a7145870db3b39c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{silver}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> matrix for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e97e74e5ea8fd7b1ced0178ba8b78dcd8a7d60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />;\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7baf291918cbe45c396bc3a7145870db3b39c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{silver}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> matrices exist for infinitely many values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> silver matrix.\n</p><p>(a): Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a02ec7d01f0b824ec9d602259b94bd94e2aa29d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n-1 &gt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> it follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62aa704e19cd3f9c422f9082b7faf217d81ab4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\exists m \\in \\{1,2,...,2n-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" /> that is not a diagonal element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Note every appearance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is paired with precisely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> diagonal elements, and every diagonal element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is paired with precisely one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. Thus, the number of diagonal elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is even. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be even if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(b): We will show if a silver matrix exists for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> then one exists for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. Consider the matrix\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b8f50c4ee3bb6a220f6b94b99c25f7cc7f30b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = \\begin{bmatrix} M &amp; M_1 \\\\  M_2 &amp; M \\end{bmatrix}\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"42\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aafa5f0474391d50c80f6bb17489bbd79cc867f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_1 = \\big((i+j-2 \\mod n) + 2n\\big)_{i,j=1}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"289\" height=\"28\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/99975108d4634e9b6776c2a9db8a8f5d32a87213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_2 = \\big((i+j-2 \\mod n) + 3n\\big)_{i,j=1}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"289\" height=\"28\" />. Fix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/8/b188e663dd23fbbbee8fead63785927bbc8378b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\{1,...,2n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" />. Then the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th column and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th row contain: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d583631fe7916a9480d14eed799d782464a2bf8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,...,2n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"17\" /> due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4fe46fe12e49b61afe45526aa4d662856772b0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n,2n+1,...,3n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"17\" /> due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6a4a0680d4e0668219585d856c7f109cd09f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313fc5aa99b898319a9d4912014fc017e4945b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n,3n+1,...,4n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"17\" /> due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c879631d01bcc51ec112e4a32a039f624d40c91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a silver matrix. Since a silver matrix clearly exists for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c1a4fc518f735825987e8be3102f51daaf40bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1, n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" /> it follows there are infinite silver matrices.\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO\" title=\"1997 IMO\">1997 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190618\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 240/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser func